mantle rm548
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_sigrun_thornbury
title the seed capital
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=chatty temper=nervy
traits temper=nervy talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk saves_blackberry_seeds_as_the_first_stock_of_a_market_stall
likes blackberries dice festival_bells misty_dawns
dislikes rats smoke
fears opening_a_stall_before_the_first_sale rats_among_the_stock
hopes a_stall_on_the_commons enough_coppers_for_a_sound_canopy
topics prices +0.5 pastimes +0.4 food +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=discreet refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# saves coppers for a market stall and sets out blackberry seeds on a clean saucer to practise opening for business.

words
oath! = Pips in my purse | Rats at my ribbon counter
saying! = Count the stock before ringing the bell | A pip can be the beginning of a stall
stockpip = my blackberry seed | a sample of next summer
stallroof = a crooked paper canopy | my folded awning
seedstall = my saucer market | the smallest fruit shop
dutchrow = a row of dark pips | a neat file of seeds
pricepebble = a shiny small stone | my pretend penny
tallydot = a red dot of juice | a mark for a sale
whitecounter = the saucer's clean rim | my round counter
waitcoin = a copper put by | my future stall money
clapper = my little spoon bell | the handle of my teaspoon
twoprice = a pair of sample pips | a seed in each lot

any
opinion festivals for 2 : A proper festival lets me hear the bells start before I open my little market.
opinion houses for 1 : It helps if someone with a big roof lets a very small business stay dry underneath.
opinion strangers against 1 : I'd like callers at my saucer to introduce themselves before I let anybody pick the pips up.
opinion road against 1 : My little stock rolls away when the road is stony. A table at home doesn't do that.
opinion times for 1 : I have berries to eat and an actual copper put away. That feels like quite a decent beginning.
opinion watch for 1 : I'd welcome some help if somebody upset my whole little shop on purpose.

grown

grown
line greet : My counter has a space in which a visitor may put an elbow.
line greet.return : Your voice has quite distinct purchasing power here.
line again.open : We've opened for another conversation.
line farewell : Save your next copper for something you want.
line farewell.return : I'll bring this little account to order.
line react.news : Could you give the part on which the price depends?
line preclose : I can close the stall with easy thoughts now.

adolescent
line greet : I've space beside my first list of prices.
line greet.return : Your greeting nearly shook my model canopy open.
line farewell : See whether the awning holds on your way past.
line farewell.return : I'll count the loose change after closing.

young
line greet : I have a saucer shop and you can stand right here.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome to the looking side of my counter.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : My little market's open as soon as the pip casts a shadow.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : I can keep one berry back for evening callers.
line greet [self.working=yes] : The figures must stay where I put them for my lesson.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family's welcome to look behind the paper roof.
line again.open : My shop recognises a returning pair of ears.
line greet.return : Heard you quite clearly over my shop bell.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar customer may have the nearest seat.
line farewell : Please leave the pips lying in their little rows.
line farewell.return : I'll look after the stock till you come round.
line react.news : Would that bit of news change a seller's mind?
line react.news.new : That's going in my little book of first occurrences.
line react.news.known : I've a pip set aside for that one already.
line react.news.doubt : Did the seller actually put the price there?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd let a sad wolf have the quiet saucer.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd ring my spoon lightly to celebrate that.
line answer.how : Worrying about the roof. Otherwise extremely busy with nothing.
line ask.how : Did you see a likely pitch for my tiny stall?
line sympathise : My shop can be shut if you'd like the bench to yourself.
line reassure : I'll keep the time by my spoon till you're ready.
line decline : I have a proper promise to keep this stock accounted for.
line accept_decline : Then that particular purchase can be postponed a little.
line thank : You've saved me a great deal of counting again.
line preclose : I need to open the paper roof for some air.
line ack : Counted twice.

young

scene seeds
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm starting a stall with blackberry pips because I can afford to own every single one.
b : Are you selling them? | Who eats the stock?
a : In my game. A real buyer would get an actual berry with the seed still inside. | I ate the part that wasn't fit to keep. That's a sensible way to acquire a sample.

scene shade
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A paper roof turns the whole saucer grey except for a bright white rim.
b : How do the customers see? | Can rain get in?
a : The front's open. Even my smallest pip should be allowed to look at its own price. | Much too easily. This is my fine-weather shop, which opens indoors.

scene lessons
when topic=work self.job=child self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can practise counting with the seeds placed exactly where the sums would go.
b : What if one rolls? | Do you count the saucer?
a : I catch it and reopen the question. That's why I prefer a proper high rim. | The saucer's the shop. It's not for sale even if the lesson runs out of things to count.

scene black
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Blackberries turn my teeth the colour of a very important seal.
b : Does it wash off? | Do you charge for that?
a : At dinner generally. I can find another berry if the seal needs renewing. | No. That's a benefit the fruit provides quite separate from my prices.

scene dice
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I roll a die to decide how many imaginary customers will call today.
b : What if you get six? | Can you get nobody?
a : I set up both sides of the saucer. That's practically a second branch of the market. | I cover the die with a cup for a private afternoon. That's the only honest way to give it no spots.

scene bells
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can open my shop on exactly the last stroke of a peal.
b : How many strokes do you wait for? | What if there's another one?
a : I usually think the last one's coming before it really does. That gives me extra practice at lifting the roof. | I say it's the opening of the other end. A round shop has room for two beginnings.

scene mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A misty dawn would be good for a stall with bright ribbon.
b : Would a ribbon show through mist? | What colour?
a : When you're close it would. The stall could be a pleasant discovery instead of making a big noise. | Something like the inside of a ripe berry. I'd see it before the paper price ticket.

scene rats
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm sure a rat would call itself my best customer and carry the saucer off without paying.
b : Is a rat big enough? | How would you stop that?
a : It might begin with my paper roof. I'd be very cross about losing the premises. | I shut the pips in a tin before bed. Purchases finish at sundown.

scene smoke
when topic=health self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When smoke makes me blink I lose track of which row I was counting.
b : Couldn't you mark the row? | Do you move away?
a : I put the spoon beside the last full one. A spoon is quite hard to overlook. | Straight to clear air. My customers have to wait for me to blink properly again.

scene father
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.father# a saucer full of stock before asking about a real stall.
b : Which part would you show first? | Will you request a loan?
a : The neat rows. I'd like it understood that I've thought about the important details. | I'm saving my own coppers first. I might ask how much a proper canopy costs.

scene high
when topic=home self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Up in the Heights I'd have an excellent distant view from my stall and very few passing feet.
b : Where would you go instead? | What about the view?
a : The Commons market once I have the money and I'm big enough to carry my counter. | I can come home to look at that. A stall needs somebody who wants a berry.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.friend# a choice of two sample lots.
b : Are the lots different? | Do friends have to pay?
a : One's got a shiny pip in the middle. I want to know whether shine affects the decision. | Not for a sample. I have read that samples are meant to help somebody choose.

scene stranger
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A new caller at my shop may look at the pips as long as the saucer stays level.
b : Can the caller touch one? | Does a caller need a name?
a : After I count them. They'd all go rolling if I had both paws busy welcoming somebody. | Only if the caller wants me to put a purchase aside. Otherwise the berries don't require a formal introduction.

scene money
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich|comfortable
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The copper in my actual fund isn't one of the shiny pebbles in my pretend till.
b : Do you get them mixed? | Why keep both?
a : I keep the copper wrapped in a little square. Metal doesn't turn up at my saucer and pretend it's a stone. | I should like to play all afternoon without accidentally selling anything I need for later.

scene visit
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd have a real sign above a market stall with a berry showing over a customer's shoulder.
b : What would it say? | How big is big?
a : I'd paint the berry and put the price below. Most wolves don't require an explanation of a blackberry. | Bigger than my nose. Something small enough for a bird to steal wouldn't be much use.

scene owes
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember when somebody lends me a shiny pebble even if the pebble looks very ordinary later.
b : Must you give the exact pebble back? | Could the lender slip your mind?
a : Certainly. An entirely similar stone isn't the particular stone we agreed about. | That's why I repeat the agreement while looking straight at the lender. It makes a sticking place in my thoughts.

scene dusk
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At closing time I tip the pips into a little fold of clean paper.
b : Won't they escape? | Why not put the whole shop away?
a : The corners tuck one inside the other. I checked the outgoing and returning numbers to make sure. | The saucer's a saucer again once the market closes. It might be needed under a cup.

adolescent

scene sums
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first tallies looked like leafless hedges. I've learned to leave decent spaces between a sum and its neighbour.
b : What's the benefit? | Do you keep the old tallies?
a : A customer can see which article belongs to which figure without asking me to read it twice. | Two early ones. They remind me that plain writing was once a thing I had to practise.

scene ribbon
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have a ribbon sample that makes an awning look expensive without improving its resistance to rain.
b : Would you buy the ribbon? | Does a sample give enough evidence?
a : After the waterproof part. I prefer that customers get their fruit and go home quite dry. | Not entirely. I'd test the seam with actual water before ordering.

scene candlemist
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In fog I'd rather hang a bright price card than shout a price at every passerby.
b : Will a card be seen? | What if they ask?
a : Once the passerby's near enough to be interested. That seems precisely the right distance. | I can give a very clear answer when somebody wants one.

grown

scene capital
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For a time my entire stock in trade would fit on a saucer and leave room for a spoon.
b : What were you selling? | Did it turn a profit?
a : Blackberry pips stood for entire lots of imaginary fruit. The smallest traders need a little imagination for capital. | It taught me which half of a transaction requires the most listening. That dividend has stayed with me.

scene shelter
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've always fancied a stall with sufficient awning to protect a waiting customer too.
b : Wouldn't that cost more? | What does the waiting customer gain?
a : A little in cloth. An overhang wide enough for one caller could turn a damp hesitation into a comfortable purchase. | Time to look at an article without rain making the choice seem urgent.

scene berryripe
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd price the fruit that should be eaten now separately from the fruit fit to travel.
b : Both ripe? | Which would you keep?
a : Ripe to the eye perhaps. One bruises under its own neighbour and one still holds a firm edge. | The soft lot for supper and the firmer fruit to send a friend tomorrow.

scene debt
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember favours distinctly and try not to confuse them with business debts.
b : Can you settle a favour? | Why keep them distinct?
a : With kindness when an occasion offers. I wouldn't present a friend with an itemised account. | One has a sum agreed. The other still has room for a generous thought.

scene turn
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A light band along one side of a mist tells me where the sun will soon show.
b : Would you set up there? | Does the mist spoil a display?
a : I should first ask where the wind comes across the market. Brightness can't keep a poor canopy from leaking. | It softens the colours. A bit of clear dark fruit on a white cloth still carries remarkably well.

scene quiet
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the pause after the bells I still catch myself hoping for one more stroke.
b : Would another bell be better? | Which sound are you waiting on?
a : Not better, quite simply more. I've kept a generous appetite for a well-shaped sound. | The end of the first sound before the next takes its place. It's longer than one ordinarily notices.

scene moneyreal
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A reserve fund only proves its value when the day calls for an unanticipated expense.
b : What qualifies? | Where would you begin again?
a : A torn awning before rain. A finer painted sign can generally wait its proper turn. | With the least copper left after covering my obligations. I've had cheerful beginnings considerably smaller than that.

scene dicegrown
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I use a throw of dice for amusement where nobody will have to make a living from the answer.
b : Does that limit the stake? | Who picks the game?
a : Happily. I'd like the losing player to finish with funds and a good appetite for supper. | A guest, provided the board sits level and the rules are clear to every player.

scene ratproof
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The best compliment I can give a well-stocked pantry is to keep the door shut after visiting.
b : Even for a short errand? | Why say compliment?
a : A rat has short errands too, and plans them according to quite a different clock. | Because somebody thought about tomorrow before putting that food by. I wish to respect the trouble.

scene merchantlook
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave visitors room to study an item before being invited to commit to it.
b : Wouldn't a prompt word help? | How would you signal welcome?
a : A plain welcome helps. A sales speech can wait on a politely expressed interest. | An open view over the counter and time to answer the first small question honestly.

scene richroom
when topic=home self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From the Heights I can overlook the entire market roof and none of the difficult work beneath it.
b : Would you rather see the work? | What's the appeal of the roof?
a : I'd go down and ask if anybody wished to show it. A distant point of view ought to recognise its limits. | The long outline resembles my earliest folded paper awning.

scene closing
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk I like to gather small loose objects before the shadows flatten out.
b : What happens if you wait? | Where do they go?
a : A perfectly bright copper can spend the evening successfully impersonating the timber's darkest knot. | Into a separate bag till morning lets me sort the pieces by appearance.

young

story sixshop [topic=pastimes]
  : I rolled a six when the shop had only five pips out on the saucer.
  : I dug in my pocket and discovered the sixth customer would have to be a very patient wolf indeed.
  b : Did you find a pip?
  : I offered to take an order for tomorrow instead. My first big day finished without a single cross customer.

story stallsail [topic=weather]
  : A breath of wind caught my store roof while I was arranging the far row of pips.
  : The paper slid across the saucer and stood upright in my empty cup.
  b : Did the stall stay open?
  : I told my imaginary callers the stall included a very small upstairs room. Then I restored my roof to its proper height.

story bellberry [topic=festival]
  : I tried ringing my spoon on the saucer to open the stall when I heard a festival bell.
  : Three pips jumped over the rim and made a little queue outside my own shop.
  b : What did the queue want?
  : To get back on the counter, I suppose. I opened quietly with my finger next time.

young

rule @lessons
when concept=bark self.job=child self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Stock in lines of three till the sum is done. | Ring softly for the end of this lesson.

rule @berry
when concept=bark self.likes=blackberries
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One lovely pip for the display row. | Dark berries under the little roof.

rule @rat
when concept=bark self.dislikes=rats
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Tin shut before rats claim a discount. | Close the shop before the paws come out.

rule @dawn
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mist outside and the counter nearly ready. | Morning price for a pretend first customer.

young
dlg resident.hub : You can see everything on this saucer from where you're standing.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : There's a familiar face above my paper shop, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I need the pips to stay inside their own rows till I know your business.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : One little spot of lamp light keeps the paper shop open.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I'm finding out how to add up a whole day's berries.
dlg resident.job : I can look after a stall not much wider than my paw.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Something just came round to my counter. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : I shall close up and lend the saucer back to tea.

young

graft @seedcapital resident.hub
choice What could I buy at a shop this small? -> seedcapital
node seedcapital
say An imaginary lot of blackberries. I've eaten the real fruit so I could lay the seeds out neatly for practice.
choice What does your first customer need? -> seedcapital_more
choice Look at the sample seeds. -> hub
node seedcapital_more
say One shiny pebble to make a purchase and patience about receiving the fruit. All the real coppers go in my other purse for a proper stall.
choice Look at the sample seeds. -> hub
choice Let the shop close. -> bye
